  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comoros - Accelerated Access to Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) MPA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increase access to climate-resilient drinking water supply, sanitation and hygiene services in Comoros, and strengthen sector governance</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will build on investments being made under the current water Project for resilience and water security for Comoros. It will expand the current scope  and include both water and sanitation investments, and geographically expand beyond the capital city of Moroni to  include investments in Anjouan and Moheli islands. Building on the pillars of the parent MPA, the project will have a deliberate focus on leveraging regional knowledge and innovation to enhance sector reforms, governance and service delivery. The project will also support preparatory activities for potential interventions on solid waste management, which negatively impacts water quality, human health and  tourism, all of which are critical elements for prosperity.</narrative>
  </description>
